Gloss:  
Kidbä mołin nesiq — After they had gone to the village;  
žeda k’eneč’yozałäy raɣruni xexoybi t’or rownäy — the woman who had been taken away by the man who had come to the village;  
mekoyn räxuƛin — the man who had come to the village;  
eƛo mi xanqor — he said to her;  
ele enza ɣˤulaz zarbazałäygon mi žedar teƛanix muhub

Gloss:  
Yedu där ħažat roqxosiƛin — when they saw the dragon’s teeth;  
q’ˤidayn risno yeženi esiya — the older brother was helping;  
qˤirič’ k’emot’ya šeƛ’ureł teł eqerno — he gave his hand to the younger one so that he might escape.

A translation for this Gitksan sentence in English is: ###When they saw the dragon’s teeth, the older brother was helping the younger one by giving his hand so that he might escape.###

Gloss:  
Bara ɣunoxorno yik’in — when they went away;  
gonda tełxor akrošawt’ani magalazas čantan kurno — the old man said to them: “You must not go”;  
riynoxuq nełar ħažataw — he warned them with a stern voice;  
q’ʷarʕaraw łinałäyn esirno — and he told them to be careful.

