tusnaq’ä yałru dikinwa necet’a ixiw muši kurxanuƛin — and when he grew up, he was very strong and brave;  
žoyä bayan bisnosi — he was the only son;  
neła hemedur q’ˤano t’umi bayräsi yoł — his father said to him: “Go to the village”;  
žedałäy nasi guluči — he took his stick;  
nasi a

Gloss:  
P’estow anusi — when they came to the house;  
xalq’i kecnaƛin — the people who had come;  
maħorno yoqno — were sitting in the house;  
yezu-yoƛ’ˤun — they were talking;  
boƛik’u xalq’i kecani — the people who had come;  
boqzaƛ’ — were sitting;  
yutin idurno nexno — they were eating;  
dahawgon q’ˤidan yičin — they were drinking;  
sos

Gloss:  
Ža täqrun — When the time came;  
ganƛ’on zown ik’in — the boy’s mother;  
zawruni uži — his three sons;  
t’umin boqno — begged the dragon;  
bik’in xanzo — after they had gone;  
kidbez akix heqno — they were not yet ready.

A translation for this Gitksan sentence in English is: ###When the time came, the boy’s mother begged the dragon, but after they had gone, they were not yet ready.###

Gloss:  
Nesä esirno — when they went outside;  
aɣikin — the wife;  
bayxanuzo — asked her husband;  
yiła — "what";  
gogaƛ’or — might those;  
mežigon — mules;  
nazay — and the wares;  
t’or rayäƛin — on them be?  

A translation for this Gitksan sentence in English is: ###When they went outside, the wife asked her husband: "What might those mules and the wares on them be?"###

Gloss:  
Łox äƛirugon — they went over the mountains;  
debez yäxuruni eniwderno ik’in — they were carrying the box with the gold inside;  
nełaq esir — the wife said;  
mesedyos mač’an — they found the box;  
tupin — they opened it;  
ašunin na mečoƛ’ eqräsiƛinno — they saw the gold inside;  
mi alžanayä — if you want;  
žuržaħayä yołƛin — you must take

Gloss:  
Way ʕabdalƛin — the man who had been away;  
eƛin ɣʷˤadä — he said;  
ʕonodkin nece yečiw ačit’ rigzaxay yoƛ’ˤuxanusi — “I will not let you go until you have told me the truth about what happened to you”;  
maħin rok’no ziruq žaya yˤoƛ’uxƛin — “I will not let you go until you have told me the truth about what happened to you.”

