Gloss:  
Eƛuk’ya tełäy bišʷan roɣno — the old man said to the boy;  
eniya badiruni magalu bac’anixƛin — when he saw the beautiful girl;  
yisä boƛƛo becarun — he wanted to take her;  
mesedyos bašiqˤoy roƛixno — and so they went to the marriage.

###The old man said to the boy: When he saw the beautiful girl, he wanted to take her, and so they went to the marriage.###

Gloss:  
Ečrut’anibin — the old man said;  
Tabuldin — to Tabuldin;  
sis haq’u — his sons;  
biłe ciqqo — were born;  
bercinaw — when they were young;  
t’abiʕatyoł ʕumrun — they were still children;  
maʕišatno bodix bičin — and lived happily ever after.

###The old man said to Tabuldin: "Your sons were born when they were young, still children, and lived happily ever after."###
